Enhancement: Add `prune --repack-group-by` to keep metadata of groups together

After `prune` repacked tree blobs, the metadata of many hosts was mixed in
shared pack files. As the local cache stores whole metadata pack files,
clients had to download much more than their own metadata after each prune.

With `prune --repack-group-by host,paths`, restic now stores the tree blobs of
each snapshot group in separate pack files. The value should match the clients'
`backup --group-by`. Without the option `prune` behaves as before.

